('Herbs of Gold', 'Calcium K2 with D3', 'supplement', ARRAY['Calcified Lithothamnion tophiforme (AquaminTM) 396mg','Calcium citrate tetrahydrate 125mg','Menaquinone 7 (vitamin K2 as K2VITALTM Delta) 15micrograms','Colecalciferol 8.3micrograms']::text[], ARRAY['Highly bioavailable calcium','Vitamin K2 binds calcium to bone','Highly bioavailable calcium','Vitamin K2 binds calcium to bone','Highly bioavailable calcium','Vitamin K2 binds calcium to bone','Highly bioavailable calcium','Vitamin K2 binds calcium to bone','calcium support, bone health, vitamin d support']::text[], ARRAY['Calcium supplementation is contraindicated in hypercalcaemia and hypercalciuria.','Caution with hyperparathyroidism and chronic kidney disease calcium supplementation should only be taken under medical supervision.','Vitamin D is contraindicated in people with vitamin D hypersensitivity, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and hypercalcaemia.','Calcium supplementation is contraindicated in hypercalcaemia and hypercalciuria.','Caution with hyperparathyroidism and chronic kidney disease calcium supplementation should only be taken under medical supervision.','Vitamin D is contraindicated in people with vitamin D hypersensitivity, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and hypercalcaemia.','Calcium supplementation is contraindicated in hypercalcaemia and hypercalciuria.','Caution with hyperparathyroidism and chronic kidney disease calcium supplementation should only be taken under medical supervision.','Vitamin D is contraindicated in people with vitamin D hypersensitivity, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and hypercalcaemia.','Calcium supplementation is contraindicated in hypercalcaemia and hypercalciuria.','Caution with hyperparathyroidism and chronic kidney disease calcium supplementation should only be taken under medical supervision.','Vitamin D is contraindicated in people with vitamin D hypersensitivity, systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and hypercalcaemia.']::text[], ARRAY['90 / 180 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0016', ARRAY['calcium_support','bone_health','vitamin_d_support']::text[], ARRAY['tetracycline_antibiotic','quinolone_antibiotic','bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','renal_impairment_caution','hypercalcaemia_caution','sarcoidosis_caution','hyperparathyroidism_caution','renal_impairment_caution']::text[], ARRAY['bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','quinolone_antibiotic','tetracycline_antibiotic']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Candida Relief', 'supplement', ARRAY['Handroanthus impetiginosus (Pau d’arco) inner stem bark extract 250mg']::text[], ARRAY['Pau d’arco, also known as Red Lapacho or Taheebo, is a canopy tree native to the Amazon rainforest and can be found in tropical regions of South and Central America. Pau d’arco has been used by native Americans of Brazil, northern Argentina, Paraguay and Peru for over','1000 years, with a long history of medicinal use that pre-dates the Incas.','The bark of the Pau d’arco tree is hard and durable and well-known for its resistance to insect and fungal attack.','Pau d’arco is traditionally used in South American medicine to relieve symptoms of mild, superficial fungal skin infections. Traditionally, the bark/heartwood of Pau d’arco was prepared as a decoction or herbal tea and was prescribed for many ailments including fevers, sore throats, dysentery and snakebites as well as used topically for wounds and skin conditions.','Pau d’arco is also traditionally used in South American medicine to support gastrointestinal system health.','The inner stem bark of Pau d’arco naturally contains bioactive compounds called naphthoquinones and furanonapthoquinones that contribute significantly to the therapeutic activity of the herb.','Two main bioactive components have been isolated from Pau d’arco: lapachol and β-lapachone. These are key constituents responsible for the antifungal and antibacterial activity of Pau d’arco. The majority','of research has focused on the lapachol component, however, other napthoquinones and their furano derivatives are likely to contribute to the therapeutic activity of Pau d’arco.','Candida Relief contains Pau d’arco sourced from Brazil that has been HPLC tested for lapachol content to identify the plant species. Pau d’arco is commonly found to contain adulterants, so proper herbal identification and quality testing is essential.','Candida','Candida albicans (Candida) is a yeast-like fungus that normally inhabits the human microbiome, is present in small amounts on the skin and can be found in the mouth, digestive and reproductive tract.','Candida is a harmless, commensal yeast that exists in harmony with other yeasts and bacteria and is only considered a fungal pathogen when there is an overgrowth in certain areas of the body.','Candida overgrowth can lead to a condition called candidiasis. There are several types of candidiasis, the most common being:','Oral/oropharyngeal/oesophageal thrush: yeast infection in the mouth, throat and oesophageal area. Symptoms include white spots inside the mouth and on the tongue, redness, soreness and difficulty swallowing.','Genital thrush: most commonly experienced by women and characterised by extreme itching, soreness and redness in the vaginal area, accompanied by white clumpy vaginal discharge.','In men, the symptoms include a red rash on the penis and itching and burning on the tip of the penis.','A number of factors can lead to candida overgrowth including disruption to the pH of the environment, antibiotic use, a weakened immune system and immunosuppressants.','Antifungal activity','Pau d’arco supports healthy immune system function and relieves the symptoms of candida. Pau d’arco and its constituents lapachol and β-lapachone have demonstrated in vitro activity against various Candida species including Candida albicans and Candida tropicalis1. Bark extracts of Pau d’arco have also shown broad-spectrum activity in vitro, specifically active against most fungal strains2.','The mechanism of action may involve interference with the fungal cell membrane3. Napthoquinones are inhibitors of the electron transport chain and act by uncoupling oxidative phosphorylation, thus inhibiting ATP synthesis.','Several constituents found in Pau d’arco have also demonstrated antibacterial activity in vitro, including lapachol, β-lapachone and anthraquinone-2-carboxylic acid. These isolated compounds have shown activity against Helicobacter pylori, Clostridium perfringens, Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Streptococcus faecalis, Enterococcus and Bacillus species, and various strains of Staphylococcus aureus4,5.','β-lapachone and other napthoquinone compounds have shown activity against methicillin-resistant staphylococcus aureus (MRSA), offering a potential synergistic effect with antimicrobial drugs6.','Pau d’arco 1000mg	✓ Supports immune health	✓ Relieves symptoms of candida']::text[], ARRAY['Contraindicated in pregnancy and lactation - Pau d’arco may cause foetal damage.','May increase the risk of bleeding. Discontinue use 2 weeks prior to surgery.']::text[], ARRAY['60 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0017', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['pregnancy_review_required','breastfeeding_review_required','surgery_caution']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
