('Herbs of Gold', 'Niacin 100mg Extended Release', 'supplement', ARRAY['Nicotinic acid (niacin) (vitamin B3) 100mg']::text[], ARRAY['Niacin is a water-soluble vitamin required for the function of over 200 enzymes throughout the body. It is well-absorbed after oral administration and metabolised in the liver to nicotinamide','adenine dinucleotide (NAD) and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADP). NAD and NADP are essential for energy metabolism, oxidation-reduction reactions and ADP-ribose transfer reactions involved in DNA repair and calcium mobilisation.','Niacin can be formed in the body from the amino acid tryptophan. It takes 60mg of tryptophan to make 1mg niacin. Poor protein intake, especially inadequate tryptophan, increases the risk of deficiency.','Niacin helps convert food into energy and assists in the metabolism of carbohydrates and dietary fats. It is a component of the glucose tolerance factor (GTF) that supports sugar metabolism.','Niacin supports skin health. It can dilate small blood vessels, improving blood flow of nutrients and oxygen to the skin, heart and brain.','Niacin is often used in high doses to maintain cardiovascular health and a healthy lipid profile. Niacin can reduce fibrinogen','concentrations in plasma and may stimulate fibrinolysis. It inhibits the mobilisation of free fatty acids from peripheral tissues and reduces hepatic synthesis of triglycerides and the secretion of low density lipoproteins and very low-density lipoproteins1.','Niacin vs nicotinamide','Two main forms of vitamin B3 are found in foods: nicotinic acid (niacin) and nicotinamide (niacinamide). Both can be converted into active forms of vitamin B3 in the body.','Both niacin and nicotinamide can perform all the essential biochemical functions of vitamin B3 in the body and prevent a deficiency, however, niacin has additional actions, such as cardiovascular effects and blood vessel dilation.','Nicotinamide does not cause the flush that is a common side effect of niacin supplementation.','Niacin flush','Niacin supplementation is commonly associated with flushing of the skin, known as the ‘niacin flush’, caused by the dilation of the capillaries. Although this effect is transient and harmless, it can be uncomfortable and concerning if people do not expect it.','The body usually adapts to niacin intake overtime and side-effects lessen in severity. Skin flushing is worse when niacin is taken on an empty stomach.','Flushing is usually caused by higher doses and immediate release niacin. Niacin 100mg Extended Release is unlikely to cause flushing.','Extended release','Niacin 100mg Extended Release is an extended-release product that releases niacin into the body over an 8-hour period. Extended-release forms are less likely to cause flushing than immediate-release forms.','It is important to differentiate extended-release from sustained-release forms. Sustained-release niacin preparations release niacin into the body over a 24-hour period and are associated with a higher risk of hepatotoxicity and gastrointestinal intolerance than unmodified niacin preparations. This may be because the liver is not given a break.','Extended-release niacin allows the vitamin to be absorbed over 8 hours, which reduces the incidence of flushing seen with immediate-release forms, and hepatotoxicity, seen with sustained-release forms, as it still allows the liver to have a break. Increased risk of hepatotoxicity is not seen with extended-release niacin2.','60 modified release tablets']::text[], ARRAY['Not recommended during pregnancy or lactation due to insufficient safety data on high doses of niacin.','Avoid consuming with alcohol. Alcohol can exacerbate the flushing associated with niacin.','Contraindicated in people with gout. Niacin can reduce urinary excretion of uric acid, potentially resulting in hyperuricemia.','Caution in people with blood sugar imbalance. High doses of niacin can impair glucose tolerance. However, doses under 1.5g daily have minimal effects on blood glucose.']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0065', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['pregnancy_review_required','breastfeeding_review_required']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
