('Herbs of Gold', 'Ubiquinol 150mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Ubiquinol-10 (Kaneka QHTM Ubiquinol) 150mg']::text[], ARRAY['Metabolically active form of CoQ10','Supports cardiovascular health','Metabolically active form of CoQ10','Supports cardiovascular health','High strength','Organically bound zinc','With vitamin A, B6 & magnesium','heart health, energy support']::text[], ARRAY['None noted at the recommended dose.','None noted at the recommended dose.','Caution with high dose zinc and vitamin A in pregnancy.','Individuals with liver or renal disease, or alcoholism should use vitamin A supplements with caution.','Taking vitamin B6 at night may result in more vivid dreams.']::text[], ARRAY['30 / 60 capsules']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0094', ARRAY['heart_health','energy_support']::text[], ARRAY['pregnancy_review_required','renal_impairment_caution','liver_impairment_caution']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin B1 100mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Thiamine hydrochloride (vitamin B1) 100mg']::text[], ARRAY['Vitamin B1 (thiamine) is a water-soluble vitamin that is involved in carbohydrate metabolism and nervous system health. As body','reserves of thiamine are small, a steady intake is important to avoid deficiency. Vitamin B1 100mg helps prevent vitamin B1 deficiency.','There is approximately 30mg of thiamine in the average adult, with about half of this stored in muscle tissue. It is also found in high concentrations in the heart, liver, kidneys and brain1.','Vitamin B1 is absorbed in the small intestine. It is generally well absorbed, however, several dietary factors can decrease absorption, including alcohol, thiaminase, sulfite preservatives, high intakes of tea and coffee and folate or protein deficiency. A high alcohol intake is the greatest risk factor for thiamine deficiency, as alcohol both impairs the absorption and enhances the excretion of the vitamin, doubling the risk of deficiency.','Strenuous exercise, fever, excessive alcohol consumption, pregnancy and lactation and adolescent growth periods can increase thiamine requirements. The elderly may also have an increased requirement for thiamine.','Food sources of thiamine include meats, wheatgerm, wholegrain cereals, peas, beans and peanuts, milk, Brewer’s yeast and yeast extracts. Wheatgerm provides an important source of thiamine in the diet, however, thiamine is sensitive to heat and light, so can be lost in processing.','Thiamine hydrochloride is the most common form of supplemental vitamin B1. It consists of 89% thiamine and 11% hydrochloric acid.','Excess thiamine is cleared from the body via the kidneys; as such, there is no evidence of toxic effects from oral administration.','Energy','Vitamin B1 is converted to its active form in the body, thiamine pyrophosphate (TPP). TPP is a vital coenzyme in the production of energy within cells.','Vitamin B1 is required for normal digestion and the conversion of food into energy. It is a cofactor for several enzymes involved in carbohydrate catabolism, including pyruvate dehydrogenase,','transketolase and alpha-ketoglutarate. It is also involved in amino acid catabolism.','Due to its role in energy production, most of the body’s thiamine is stored in muscle.','A study found that supplementation with 10mg thiamine daily in women with a marginal deficiency lead to significantly increased general well-being and decreased fatigue2.','Nervous system','Vitamin B1 is important to maintain a healthy nervous system. It is located in the nerve cell membrane and is important for the transmission of nerve impulses.','Vitamin B1 plays a role in the metabolism of several neurotransmitters, including acetylcholine, GABA and serotonin, and, therefore, plays a role in maintaining healthy mood.','Hormones','A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled crossover study found that 100mg of vitamin B1 daily helped the symptoms of dysmenorrhoea and supplementation had lasting effects up to 3 months after the supplementation3.']::text[], ARRAY['None noted at the recommended dose.']::text[], ARRAY['100 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0095', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin B2 200mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Riboflavin (vitamin B2) 200mg']::text[], ARRAY['Vitamin B2 (riboflavin) is a water-soluble B vitamin that helps maintain the integrity of mucous membranes, skin, eyes and the nervous system.','Riboflavin is mostly present in the body as a component of two coenzymes: Flavin mononucleotide (FMN) and Flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD).','Common clinical symptoms of riboflavin deficiency include inflammation of the throat, mouth (stomatitis), and tongue (glossitis); cracking of the tissue around the corners of the mouth (angular cheilitis) and moist, red, scaly skin.','Vitamin B2 is essential for the activation of other B complex vitamins. FAD is required for the formation of niacin from tryptophan and FMN is required for the formation of the active vitamin B6. Vitamin B2 also participates in folate metabolism. FAD is a cofactor for','methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase (MTHRF), which converts folate into its active form.','Vitamin B2 promotes normal growth and tissue repair. It is required for the growth of skin, hair and nails and a deficiency of vitamin B2 can lengthen wound healing time.','Vitamin B2 helps maintain a healthy immune system. It is required for humoral antibody formation and helps maintain tissue barriers to infection.','Antioxidant','Migraines','Several studies have shown vitamin B2 to be an effective prophylactic to reduce the incidence of migraines.','A preliminary open pilot study of 49 patients with migraine (45 without aura, 4 with aura) found 400mg of riboflavin with or without aspirin for 3 months resulted in a 68.2% improvement in migraine severity. Eighty percent of patients treated with riboflavin alone had a 50% or greater reduction in monthly migraine days1.','Following this, a double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled study investigated the effects of 400mg riboflavin or placebo daily for 3 months on 55 patients with migraine. Riboflavin was found to be superior to placebo in reducing attack frequency (p=0.005) and headache days (p=0.012). For headache days, the number of patient responders (at least 50% improvement) was 15% for placebo and 59% for riboflavin (p=0.002; NNT 2.3)2.','More recently, a double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled study involving 98 patients receiving either 400mg riboflavin daily or placebo for 3 months was performed. The duration and frequency of headache were significantly less in the second and third months of the study in the riboflavin group vs placebo (p=0.012 and p=0.001, respectively)3.','A 2017 systematic review concluded that riboflavin is a well-tolerated and inexpensive treatment, demonstrating efficacy in the reduction of adult patient’s migraine headache frequency as well as duration4.','Vitamin B2 plays an important role in the body’s antioxidant defence','network. FAD is a cofactor for glutathione reductase, which recycles oxidised glutathione.','Vitamin B2, due to its role in antioxidant systems, helps maintain healthy eyes. Glutathione reductase is involved the protection of the lens from free radical damage.','Energy','FMN and FAD are involved in energy metabolism and the release of energy from nutrients in all body cells. FAD is involved in the citric acid cycle, while FMN has a role in the electron transport chain.','Vitamin B2 aids in the metabolism of carbohydrates, fats and proteins, helping to convert food into energy.','Cardiovascular health','Due to its role in folate metabolism, vitamin B2 is important for homocysteine metabolism and, therefore, helps maintain a healthy cardiovascular system.','Vitamin B2 is also important for the formation of haemoglobin which helps transport oxygen in red blood cells and, therefore, helps maintain normal blood.','There is a correlation between plasma levels of vitamin B2 and homocysteine levels, with high homocysteine levels showing low riboflavin status. High homocysteine levels are associated with a higher risk of cardiovascular conditions.','High strength	✓ Healthy eyes	✓ Energy production	✓ Mild migraine relief']::text[], ARRAY['None noted at the recommended dose.']::text[], ARRAY['60 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0096', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin B3 500mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Nicotinamide (vitamin B3) 500mg']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['Caution in pregnancy and breastfeeding – safety of high dose vitamin B3 is unknown.','Caution in individuals with gout. Large doses of vitamin B3 can reduce urinary excretion of uric acid (a risk factor for gout).','concentrations in the liver, muscles, kidneys and heart. Excess vitamin','B3 is methylated in the liver and excreted in the urine.','Vitamin B3 can be formed in the body from the amino acid tryptophan, however, it takes approximately 60mg of tryptophan to form 1mg of niacin, with an approximate conversion rate of 60:1. This conversion requires adequate iron, riboflavin and vitamin B6.','As tryptophan is also a precursor to serotonin and dietary tryptophan is preferentially converted to vitamin B3 in deficiency states, low levels of vitamin B3 can result in serotonin depletion and mood alterations.','Energy','Vitamin B3 is used in the body in two coenzyme forms – nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (NAD) and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADP), which participate in over 200 metabolic reactions.','Vitamin B3, as NAD and NADP, plays a major role in the metabolism of carbohydrate, proteins, fats and alcohol. NAD acts as an electron and hydrogen acceptor in glycolysis and the citric acid cycle. NADP is primarily involved in fatty acid biosynthesis.','Skin health','Vitamin B3, in the form of nicotinamide, supports skin health and DNA repair and has been shown to have a protective effect against damage caused by UV radiation. It prevents the ATP depletion and glycolytic blockade induced by UV radiation, boosting cellular energy and enhancing DNA repair in the skin.','A double-blind, randomised, placebo controlled crossover trial examined the effects of oral nicotinamide on UV exposure in 61 volunteers. Significant immunosuppression occurred in a UV dose-dependent manner in the presence of placebo. Oral nicotinamide, at doses of either 500mg or 1500mg daily, were well tolerated and significantly reduced UV immunosuppression with no immune effects in unirradiated skin1.','A phase 3, double-blind, randomised, controlled trial using 500mg of nicotinamide twice daily substantiated the benefits of vitamin B3 in supporting skin health and protecting skin from the damaging effects of the sun2.']::text[], ARRAY['60 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0097', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['pregnancy_review_required','breastfeeding_review_required','renal_impairment_caution','liver_impairment_caution']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin B5 500mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Calcium pantothenate 555mg']::text[], ARRAY['Vitamin B5, also known as pantothenic acid, is a water-soluble B complex vitamin that is widely distributed throughout the food chain.','Pantothenic acid gets its name from the Greek ‘panto’, which means ‘everywhere’ and refers to the ubiquitous nature of this nutrient.','Vitamin B5 is a component of coenzyme A (CoA), the biologically active form of pantothenic acid, which is involved in over 100 metabolic reactions in the body. It is essential for the breakdown of carbohydrates, proteins, lipids and alcohol, the formation of fatty acids, cholesterol, bile acids and steroid hormones, and is involved in energy metabolism.','Major dietary sources of vitamin B5 include chicken, beef, potatoes, oats, tomato products, liver, kidney, egg yolks and whole grains. Vitamin B5 is easily destroyed by food processing, including freezing, canning and refining processes.','Approximately 50% of dietary vitamin B5 is absorbed1. It is absorbed in the jejunum and excreted in the urine. There is currently no upper limit for this vitamin as no toxic effects have been reported.','Pantothenic acid is the most common supplemental form of vitamin B5. It is comprises 91.5% pantothenic acid and 7.5% calcium.','Nervous system','Vitamin B5 supports nervous system health.','CoA is a cofactor in the synthesis of the neurotransmitter acetylcholine, which is involved in learning, memory and mood.','Vitamin B5 is often referred to as the ‘anti-stress’ vitamin, as it is necessary for adrenal function and a healthy stress response. It is involved in the production of glucocorticoids and other adrenal','hormones, including cortisol. Vitamin B5 has been found to enhance adrenal cortical function in animals and may lower secretion of cortisol in periods of stress.','Skin health','Vitamin B5 helps regulate epidermal barrier function and keratinocyte differentiation via CoA metabolism and plays an essential role in normal epithelial function.','Acne is a common skin condition that affects the hair follicles associated with an oil gland. It can present with inflammatory or non-inflammatory lesions.','A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study looked at the effects of high-strength pantothenic acid in adults previously','diagnosed with mild to moderate acne vulgaris. Forty-eight subjects were randomised to pantothenic acid (2.2g) or placebo for 12 weeks. There was a significant mean reduction in total lesion count in the pantothenic acid group versus placebo at week 12 (p=0.0197)2.','Another open-label, single arm study in 10 healthy adults diagnosed with mild to moderate acne found that pantothenic acid reduced the number of facial skin blemishes by 56% after 8 weeks3.','calcium support, bone health']::text[], ARRAY['Caution in pregnancy and breastfeeding – safety of high dose vitamin B5 is unknown']::text[], ARRAY['60 capsules']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0098', ARRAY['calcium_support','bone_health']::text[], ARRAY['tetracycline_antibiotic','quinolone_antibiotic','bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','renal_impairment_caution','pregnancy_review_required','breastfeeding_review_required']::text[], ARRAY['bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','quinolone_antibiotic','tetracycline_antibiotic']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin B6 100mg', 'supplement', ARRAY['Pyridoxine hydrochloride 85mg','Pyridoxal 5-phosphate monohydrate 47mg']::text[], ARRAY['High strength','With activated B6','High strength','With activated B6']::text[], ARRAY['Taking vitamin B6 at night may result in more vivid dreams.','Taking vitamin B6 at night may result in more vivid dreams.']::text[], ARRAY['60 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0099', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin C 1000 Plus', 'supplement', ARRAY['Calcium ascorbate dihydrate 605.3mg','Sodium ascorbate 562.4mg','Citrus bioflavonoids extract 50mg','Zinc amino acid chelate 8mg','Rutoside (rutin) 5mg','Hesperidin 5mg']::text[], ARRAY['High dose vitamin C','Low acid formula','Immune health','High dose vitamin C','Low acid formula','Immune health','calcium support, bone health, immune support, skin health, hair nail support, antioxidant support']::text[], ARRAY['Use in caution if there is a history of renal impairment or renal calculi (kidney stones) as vitamin C (ascorbic acid) may increase the risk of recurrence of calcium oxalate calculi.','Caution in iron overload conditions, such as haemochromatosis, as vitamin C can increase iron absorption.','Use in caution if there is a history of renal impairment or renal calculi (kidney stones) as vitamin C (ascorbic acid) may increase the risk of recurrence of calcium oxalate calculi.','Caution in iron overload conditions, such as haemochromatosis, as vitamin C can increase iron absorption.']::text[], ARRAY['60 / 120 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0100', ARRAY['calcium_support','bone_health','immune_support','skin_health','hair_nail_support','antioxidant_support']::text[], ARRAY['tetracycline_antibiotic','quinolone_antibiotic','bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','renal_impairment_caution','penicillamine','renal_impairment_caution']::text[], ARRAY['bisphosphonate','levothyroxine','penicillamine','quinolone_antibiotic','tetracycline_antibiotic']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin D3 1000', 'supplement', ARRAY['Colecalciferol 25micrograms']::text[], ARRAY['Vegan friendly','Aids bone mineralisation','Assists with calcium absorption','vitamin d support, bone health']::text[], ARRAY['Contraindicated in sarcoidosis or hyperparathyroidism without medical supervision.']::text[], ARRAY['120 / 240 capsules']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0101', ARRAY['vitamin_d_support','bone_health']::text[], ARRAY['hypercalcaemia_caution','renal_impairment_caution','sarcoidosis_caution','hyperparathyroidism_caution']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitamin K2 180 MAX', 'supplement', ARRAY['Menaquinone 7 (vitamin K2)(K2VITAL™) 180micrograms']::text[], ARRAY['High-strength vitamin K2','K2VITAL™','All-trans MK-7','Supports bone strength','High-strength vitamin K2','K2VITAL™','All-trans MK-7','Supports bone strength','bone health']::text[], ARRAY['None noted at the recommended dose.']::text[], ARRAY['60 capsules']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0102', ARRAY['bone_health']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[]),
('Herbs of Gold', 'Vitex 1000', 'supplement', ARRAY['Vitex agnus-castus (Chaste tree) fruit extract 100mg']::text[], ARRAY['Vitex agnus-castus (Chaste tree) has a long history of traditional use in Western herbal medicine (WHM) for the relief of menstrual irregularities and symptoms of premenstrual tension (PMT).','The dried fruit from the Vitex plant contains several active constituents including flavonoids, iridoids, alkaloids and volatile oils.','The mode of action of Vitex is multifaceted. Vitex acts on dopamine (D2) receptors in the anterior pituitary gland, decreasing high prolactin levels. Prolactin is a hormone that primarily functions to help women produce milk after childbirth. However, in non-breastfeeding mothers, elevated prolactin can block the production of other hormones in the body, including oestrogen and progesterone. Elevated prolactin levels are associated with menstrual irregularities and symptoms of PMT1.','Low doses of Vitex have been shown to increase luteinising hormone (LH) while decreasing follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH), working indirectly on achieving oestrogen and progesterone balance within the body. Oestrogen dominance in females is linked to mood disorders, including PMS, and menstrual irregularities.','It is recommended Vitex be taken in the morning, before breakfast, as this is the time the pituitary gland is the most receptive.','Premenstrual syndrome','Premenstrual syndrome (PMS) is a combination of emotional, physical, psychological and mood disturbances that generally occur after a female ovulates and before the onset of a menstrual period.','Emotional symptoms can include irritability, crying, oversensitivity and mood swings, while physical symptoms may present as fatigue, bloating, breast tenderness, skin issues such as acne or appetite changes and food cravings.','It is estimated that as many as 90% of women experience at least one PMS symptom most months and about 50% of women experience several PMS symptoms each month2.','For some women who suffer from PMS, the symptoms are severe enough to interfere with regular day-to-day activities.','Vitex 1000 for PMS','Several clinical studies have been conducted on Vitex for premenstrual syndrome. A phytopharmaceutical formulation of an extract of Vitex fruit was used in 1634 females suffering from PMS symptoms. Self-assessment questionnaires were used to assess symptoms such as headache, anger, irritability, mood, breast fullness and bloating. After taking Vitex for three menstrual cycles, 93% of females reported either a decrease in the number of symptoms or complete cessation of complaints3.','A further study of 178 women with symptoms of PMS tested against placebo demonstrated a statistically significant improvement against symptoms of irritability, mood alteration, anger, headache, breast fullness and bloating4.','Trickey, R. (2011). Women, Hormones & the Menstrual Cycle (2nd ed). Allen & Unwin.','Vitex 1000 for menstrual regulation','Irregular periods can be caused by many factors, including but not limited to, sporadic ovulation, decreased progesterone or increased prolactin.','Vitex works by increasing the release of luteinizing hormone from the pituitary gland, which raises progesterone and normalises the second half of the menstrual cycle.','Vitex & the oral contraceptive pill (OCP)','Vitex is generally not considered suitable to be used alongside the OCP.','Vitex may reduce the effectiveness of contraceptives as it can act as a precursor to the hormones involved in ovulation. This may negate the ovulation-inhibiting effects of the OCP. As a result, women using Vitex alongside birth control could experience an increased risk of unplanned pregnancy5.','High strength	✓ PMS relief	✓ Menstrual cycle regulation	✓ One-a-day dose','women health, menopause review required']::text[], ARRAY['Avoid use in individuals with tumours sensitive to oestrogen or progesterone.','Vitex is not generally recommended in females under 20 years of age as the natural hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian axis can be easily disrupted.','Vitex is most effective during the first three to six months of use. After that, its effect on the pituitary starts to diminish. It is recommended to take a break from Vitex for two months before resuming use.','Not recommended during pregnancy without medical advice and breastfeeding due to insufficient studies relating to safety.']::text[], ARRAY['60 tablets']::text[], NULL, true, NULL, 'HOG-0103', ARRAY['women_health','menopause_review_required']::text[], ARRAY['pregnancy_review_required','breastfeeding_review_required']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[])
;


